course: dictionary
lesson: 3281
title: Moving stairs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An escalator is a moving staircase. It carries people up or down between floors, so you can ride instead of climbing. «On escalators in malls you hold the rail and never run up the down escalator.» The clues are moving, carries people and floors, so an escalator must be a staircase that moves.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «On moving stairs in malls you hold the rail and never run up the down moving stairs.» It still makes sense, so your meaning fits. If it did not, you would need to think again.
explain: «An escalator is a long loop of steps pulled round by a motor and gears, and the steps flatten at the ends so you can step on and off.» Flatten means the steps go level at the top and bottom, so your feet can get on and off safely.
fact: An escalator is a moving staircase that carries people up or down between floors.
fact: «An escalator is a loop of steps on a chain pulled by a motor; the steps flatten at the top and bottom, and the handrail moves at the same speed as the steps.»
fact: Escalators are found in shopping centres, airports and stations, such as on the London Underground.
fact: In the UK, stand on the right so people in a hurry can walk up on the left.
fact: Safety rules: hold the handrail, face forwards, keep shoelaces and loose clothes away from the edges, and never sit or play on an escalator.
exercise: What is an escalator? | A long rope for climbing | A lift with walls and a door | *A moving staircase that carries people between floors | A type of shop
exercise: Where might you find an escalator? | *At an airport or a station | Inside a school pencil case | At the bottom of the sea | A farm field
exercise: In the UK, why do people stand on the right of an escalator? | So the steps stay dry | So the motor can rest | *So people in a hurry can walk on the left | Because the right side is always the top
test: Which is the safest thing to do on an escalator? | Sit on the steps and wave | Play with a ball on the steps | Run up the down escalator to save time | *Hold the handrail and face forwards
test: «The steps flatten at the ends so you can step on and off.» What does flatten mean here? | *Become level, so the steps are flat | Start to move faster | Break into small pieces | Become much bigger
exam: Which word best describes an escalator? | A small dog | A type of bird | *A moving staircase | A parked car
